THE STATE APPORTIONMENT IS COMPUTED FROM AVERAGE
DAILY ATTENDANCE, NOT FROM ENROLLMENT. A PUPIL ON
THE ROLL WHO DOES NOT ATTEND EARNS NOTHING.

AN INSTRUCTIONAL DAY IS A DAY ON WHICH SCHOOL IS
IN SESSION FOR THE FULL SCHEDULED HOURS. HALF DAYS
FOR PARENT CONFERENCES COUNT AS HALF.

ADA = AGGREGATE DAYS ATTENDED / INSTRUCTIONAL DAYS,
CARRIED TO TWO PLACES, PER BUILDING AND IN TOTAL.

THE CLAIM IS DUE THE 15TH FOLLOWING EACH REPORTING
PERIOD. A LATE CLAIM IS PAID IN THE NEXT PERIOD.
